<Base title="About — Mathilde Vita Blixenkrone-Møller">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    I am a designer who builds. I live in Aarhus, and I am looking for work
    in design and frontend development.
  </p>

  <p>
    I hold a degree in IT Product Development from Aarhus University,
    finished in 2025. The work I like best sits between the two halves of
    that title: finding out what people actually need, and being able to
    build enough of it to see whether it holds up.
  </p>

  <h2>Before this</h2>

  <p>
    I trained as a sign language interpreter and worked as one from 2017 to
    2023, freelance, by the hour, and permanently employed. Interpreting is
    the work of making sure something arrives with the person it is meant
    for, in a form they can use. That is not far from what interaction
    design is about, and it is a large part of why I ended up here.
  </p>

  <p>
    ?? BRUG FOR INPUT: en eller to sætninger om, hvorfor du skiftede spor.
    Det skal være dine egne ord, ikke mine. Hold det ligefremt, det behøver
    hverken forklaring eller undskyldning.
  </p>

  <h2>Teaching</h2>

  <p>
    In the autumn of 2024 I was an instructor on the Human Computer
    Interaction course at Aarhus University. I ran the exercise sessions for
    the students and graded their assignments. Explaining a method to
    someone who is meeting it for the first time is a good test of whether
    you understand it yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>What I am looking for</h2>

  <p>
    A role where design and implementation sit close together, and where I
    get to talk to the people the work is for.
  </p>

  <p>
    ?? BRUG FOR INPUT: vil du nævne noget konkret her, for eksempel at du er
    åben for både design- og udviklerstillinger?
  </p>

